<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Sola furious at Chile beef injunction.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Sola furious at Chile beef injunction.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's Agriculture Secretary Felipe Sola Tuesday condemned a court injunction by a Chilean farm group to limit Argentine beef imports.</p>
<p>&quot;It is an outrage that this should occur after the agreement of the Uruguay Round of the GATT and in the same week that Chile joins Mercosur,&quot; Sola told farmers at a seminar.</p>
<p>Sola's office said that Chile's Agricultural Society had lodged an injunction to restrict imports of Argentine beef on grounds of quality.</p>
<p>&quot;The people getting nervous are the Chilean producers, who have meat of lower quality, with higher costs, which is why they ask for protection,&quot; Sola said.</p>
<p>Sola added that he hoped that the Chilean government would help solve the problem. He said that Argentina has 30 percent of the Chilean beef market.</p>
<p>Chile recently clinched a free-trade deal with the Mercosur customs union, which groups Argentina, Brazil, Paraguay and Uruguay.</p>
<p>-- Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 3187-0655</p>
